    "### Your explanation\n",
    "\n",
    "**What evidence supports your treatment or decision to retain the values?**\n",
    "\n",
    "I built the arrival date from year, month and day for all 119,390 raw rows and every single combination is a real calendar date (0 invalid ones, so no 31 April or 30 February), and the dates run from 1 July 2015 to 31 August 2017 as expected. The supplied `arrival_date_week_number` disagrees with the standard ISO week in 64,054 rows (54%), which looked bad at first. But when I tried other week definitions, one of them matched every row: weeks start on Sunday and week 1 is the week that contains 1 January (0 mismatches in the full file and in all three partitions). That also explains why week 53 exists in 2015 and 2016. So the column isn't wrong, it just isn't ISO, and I kept it as supplied and removed no rows. I added two helpful columns: the real `arrival_date` and `arrival_weekday` (the day of the week, which the models can use as a timing feature)."
   ]
